        "description": "Record privately. Understand the sounds of your night. Discover memorable moments.\n\nYOUR BEDTIME ROOM\nStart your night in a cozy bedroom. Arrange furniture and change the room to make it your own. Optional furniture purchases are available.\n\nGo Sleep listens while you rest and uses on-device sound analysis to organize likely snoring, speech-like events that may be sleep talking, and cough-like sounds. Silence is never intentionally stored, and detected events become short playable clips.\n\nNIGHT SOUNDS AT A GLANCE\n• Review Snoring, Possible Sleep Talking, and Cough-like Sounds separately\n• See when each sound type appeared in simple night narrative cards\n• Explore a clock-aligned event timeline and relative loudness\n• Compare patterns across nights and reported sleep positions\n\nSNORING INSIGHTS\n• Follow your 0–100 Snore Load wellness trend\n• Review detected duration, episodes, and longest events\n• Track weekly and monthly patterns without turning every sound into one sleep score\n\nDISCOVER THE FUN SIDE OF SLEEP\nHear memorable Sound Matches shared by the community. When you want to join in, you choose exactly which clip to publish. Your private night report stays unchanged.\n\nBUILT FOR PRIVACY\n• Audio analysis happens on your iPhone\n• No speech transcription is performed\n• Silence is never intentionally stored\n• Recordings stay on your device unless you enable private iCloud Sync\n• Public sharing is always an explicit choice\n\nWIDGETS AND LONG-TERM INSIGHTS\nStart a recording quickly and follow night sound activity from your Home Screen. Go Sleep Pro unlocks deeper insights, full report history, and longer clip retention. Private iCloud Sync is free for all users.\n\nPossible Sleep Talking and Cough-like Sounds are audio observations. They do not confirm who spoke and are not symptom counts or medical assessments.\n\nGo Sleep provides wellness trends and is not a medical device or diagnosis. If you are concerned about sleep apnea or breathing interruptions, speak with a healthcare professional.\n\nTerms of Use: https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/\n\nOfficial site: https://gosleep.ajigu.com/",
